# {{.ProjectName}}

A Go application built with modern Go practices and best conventions.

## Prerequisites

- Go 1.21 or higher
- Make (optional, for convenient commands)

## Installation

```bash
# Clone the repository
git clone
cd {{.ProjectName}}

# Download dependencies
go mod tidy
```

## Usage

```bash
# Run the application
go run main.go

# Or run with arguments
go run main.go --help
```

## Building

```bash
# Build for current platform
go build -o bin/{{.ProjectName}}

# Build for multiple platforms
make build-all

# Or manually:
GOOS=linux GOARCH=amd64 go build -o bin/{{.ProjectName}}-linux-amd64
GOOS=windows GOARCH=amd64 go build -o bin/{{.ProjectName}}-windows-amd64.exe
GOOS=darwin GOARCH=amd64 go build -o bin/{{.ProjectName}}-darwin-amd64
```

## Development

```bash
# Install development tools
go install github.com/air-verse/air@latest
go install golang.org/x/tools/cmd/goimports@latest

# Run with hot reload
air

# Format code
go fmt ./...
goimports -w .

# Lint code
golangci-lint run
```

## Testing

```bash
# Run all tests
go test ./...

# Run tests with coverage
go test -v -race -coverprofile=coverage.out ./...
go tool cover -html=coverage.out

# Run benchmarks
go test -bench=. ./...
```

## Project Structure

```
.
├── cmd/                    # Application entrypoints
│   └── {{.ProjectName}}/   # Main application
├── internal/               # Private application code
│   ├── config/            # Configuration
│   ├── handler/           # HTTP handlers
│   ├── service/           # Business logic
│   └── repository/        # Data access layer
├── pkg/                   # Public library code
├── api/                   # API definitions (OpenAPI/Swagger)
├── web/                   # Web UI assets
├── migrations/            # Database migrations
├── scripts/               # Build and deployment scripts
├── configs/               # Configuration files
├── test/                  # Additional external test apps and test data
├── docs/                  # Design and user documents
├── .github/               # GitHub Actions workflows
├── Dockerfile             # Container definition
├── Makefile               # Common tasks
└── README.md              # This file
```

## Configuration

The application can be configured using:

1. **Environment variables**: `{{.ProjectName | upper}}_PORT=8080`
2. **Configuration files**: `configs/config.yaml`
3. **Command-line flags**: `--port 8080`

## Docker

```bash
# Build image
docker build -t {{.ProjectName}} .

# Run container
docker run -p 8080:8080 {{.ProjectName}}

# Using docker-compose
docker-compose up
```

## API Documentation

When the server is running, visit:
- Swagger UI: `http://localhost:8080/swagger/`
- API docs: `http://localhost:8080/docs/`

